s definitely paid off  as gus's character really came to life  with the movement of his antlers and  ears  someone thinks i'm a hybrid i start  talking i never ever move my ears  how does this mechanism work you might  ask  jim mikkel one of the show's creators  commented so christian converi  basically has a little helmet which is  hair and it sits on top  the antlers click in they're amazing  they're really light they click in with  magnets  then he's got these ears that will sit  over the top of his ears  and little cables that run down his back  and he has these little motors that are  strapped to his back the whole time that  are hidden  then there's a puppeteer that operates  on him remotely they can do  all sorts of shapes and reactions and  speeds sounds complicated to me but it  turned out to be so  so worth it there are no kids like me  the only one left  that's what he told you gus was not the  only hybrid brought to life through  puppetry in this series  in fact puppetry played a pretty  significant role in bringing the idea of  hybrids to life overall  interestingly enough all of the baby  hybrids featured in episode 1  were real puppets even more impressively  the character bobby was a real-life  puppet who was controlled through  multiple talented puppeteers and a  harness system  talk about some intense teamwork the  rest of the children within the series  who were also cast as hybrids were  brought to life using intense makeup  prosthetics which highlighted very  specific  animalistic features for each of the  young actors  last dijk you were part animal too you  know  makeup artist stefan knight and his team  were able to bring these half human  creatures to life using this method  everyone knows that the casting process  in hollywood can be pretty cutthroat  for actor christian convery who plays  gus the audition process seemed to run  pretty smoothly as the young actor made  it through callbacks and landed the role  with little stress  he's bigger than you it'll make him  bigger than me  actor nonso anazi had a bit of a harder  time  in the casting process though claiming  he had to fight a bit more for the role  as many people loved the role of tommy  shepard and also wanted a shot at  playing him  they bought what i was telling him and  here i am playing tommy jennifer today  the young actor immediately began  studying the mannerisms of deer once he  landed the part in order to best prepare  for the role  researched how years move and react this  level of acting for such a young actor  is super impressive and really  noteworthy converi  is only 11 years old not only did the  child star work to perfect his  animal-like acting performance  but he also took parkour lessons to best  learn safe ways to move about like an  animal too  because deers have to run and jump  really fast all the time  this level of dedication to the acting  game is seriously  something magical if you ask me anozie  didn't have to take part in  any parkour training but had to take  fight lessons instead  as his big fight scene of the first  episode required him to have some  professional training  so that was that was pretty tough now  you might be asking yourself how did the  production team go about handling the  fact that this series is set in the  midst of a pandemic  did they take notes from the covet  outbreak that's sweeping the globe to  get their pandemic information down pat  the answer is surprisingly no the pilot  of this series was  filmed in may and june of 2019 before  the pandemic truly took a foothold  globally  before the greek crumble so what did the  production team do  to make their fictional pandemic as  accurate as they could  instead the team studied previous  outbreaks of the bird flu and sars to  get their information as close to  reality as possible  all of our science tracked when the real  pandemic started said jim mikel  one of the show's creators and  showrunners not only was the way in  which the team tackled the portrayal of  the pandemic really fantastic  but so was their fortunate decision to  shoot on location in new zealand  new zealand is a country known for its  intense and startling natural beauty  pretty much making the use of cgi or any  other digital enhancements pointless  valley of sorrows it looks pretty happy  to me  not only did this make new zealand the  perfect setting for the fantastical  series  but the way the nation was affected by  kovid also helped with little  to no shutdown the production process  that took place in 2020 was able to keep  on rolling  as anazi stated when we found out that  new zealand was one of the countries  that had got their act together the  quickest and we'd be able to shoot there  that was a very great thing from amazing  casting efforts to great scientific  research and even lucky location  scouting  it seems that the production process  behind the scenes of sweet tooth was  truly impressive which can be clearly  seen in the final product of the series  as you probably already know the team  behind the scenes of sweet tooth was  also a major reason for the series  newfound success  with robert downey jr and his wife susan  downey at the helm of the production  team  there was really no doubt that this  series was gonna be a hit  we'd like a challenge and an adventure  in this was both  the couple decided to create a much more  family-friendly version of this original  graphic novel leaving out a bit of the  gritty darkness of the series in place  of some hope  as susan downey stated the ambition was  to create it for a family audience  we wanted the whole family to be able to  watch together  rdj went on to say that the comics had  this scope and emotional breadth of  storytelling  and the characters were just so engaging  we wanted to make a great co-viewing  experience for parents and kids  just think think of the possibility sure  enough the power couple  definitely met their goal now there's no  way to talk about sweet tooth and its  adaptation into a television series  without acknowledging what the original  author has to say about it  thankfully author of the sweet tooth  graphic novel series jeff lemire has  nothing bad to say in fact when asked  about what it was like to see his comic  come to life the author said  it's pretty magical it was really  interesting to see which aspects of the  world  jim and the team latched onto and how  they leaned into the hopefulness of the  story and gus's innocence  and kind of bringing something new to it  um it's been interesting  as we can see from our behind-the-scenes  look at sweet tooth  it was really a bunch of different  factors that led the series to be the  greatness that it is  from casting choices to puppetry and  prosthetics the impressiveness of the  production process is clear  everywhere next time you're watching  sweet tooth keep all this  exclusive information in mind it will  make you appreciate the series  even more
 

